The graph plots $\log_{10}V$ against time for an investment, where $V$ is the value in dollars.
By what factor did the investment grow over the $40$ years shown?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=9cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-2,xmax=46,ymin=0,ymax=5.6,xtick={0,5,...,40},ytick={0,0.5,...,5},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (years)},ylabel={$\log_{10}V$},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:40,samples=2] {3+0.05*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
